    description: 'Detects suspected PHP2Shell-style post-exploitation behavior where a web server process starts a shell with -c and runs reconnaissance or payload staging commands such as id, whoami, curl, wget, or base64 -d. This indicates likely remote code execution leading to command execution on internet-facing infrastructure. It does not detect the initial exploit request itself when no request-level signature is available.'
